Subject: [PATCH 2/3] sidebar: toggleTabstrip without the revamp launcher

Why Firefox source must change:
  toggleTabstrip (run at init and on every tab-orientation change,
  revamp or not) unconditionally calls sidebarMain.requestUpdate(), which
  throws when the revamp launcher component was never loaded - the case once
  vertical tabs can run without the revamp (0001).

What it changes:
  - Re-render the launcher only when revamp components are loaded.
  - Guard the launcher state access on the horizontal path.

Depends on: 0001 (makes the path reachable).
Validation: aequera rail tests (orientation switches with revamp off, no
  exceptions); upstream sidebar tests unchanged.
Upstream risk: low; two guards in toggleTabstrip.

diff --git a/browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js b/browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js
index 6a9110289903..9e9bbbfee20c 100644
--- a/browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js
+++ b/browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js
@@ -2560,9 +2560,13 @@ var SidebarController = {
     );
     verticalToolbar.toggleAttribute("visible", toVerticalTabs);
     // Re-render sidebar-main so that templating is updated
-    // for proper keyboard navigation for Tools
-    this.sidebarMain.requestUpdate();
-    if (!toVerticalTabs) {
+    // for proper keyboard navigation for Tools. Without the revamp (vertical
+    // tabs hosted by the browser shell) the launcher component is never
+    // loaded, so there is nothing to re-render.
+    if (this.revampComponentsLoaded) {
+      this.sidebarMain.requestUpdate();
+    }
+    if (!toVerticalTabs && this._state) {
       // Horizontal tabs have no expanded launcher state. If the visibility pref
       // isn't changing as part of this orientation switch, launcherExpanded
       // won't be updated by its observer, so un-expand the launcher here.
